## The five PARTLY flags: four "left-out" items have rows the brief did not name; #27 opened three rows **[v3]**

The `ifiled2` briefs listed, for each passage, the id `#555` POINTS it at.  Where `#555` also FILED a new row on the
same lines, the brief named only the pointer, so agy read the pointer row, found it does not cover the rest of the
passage, and said so -- correctly, of the pointer.  The rest is covered by the new row, in the same table
(`regress/artifacts/idless_20261002/IDLESS_TABLE2.tsv`, columns id / sev / queue lines / title):

| flag | passage (db8b1a33) | pointer agy read | what agy found left out | the row that carries it (**[v3]** `#555`'s, except #28's, filed by `#554`; v1 headed this "the `#555` row") |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| ifiled2_1 #15 | 1980-1982 | `qhx11fifo` | the SCIF RDF bit never set; SSR verbatim-write; FDR width clamp | `qhscifssr` MED, lines 1980-1982: "SCIF SSR stores guest writes verbatim, the receive path maintains DR and does not generate RDF, FDR clamps the receive count at 255" |
| ifiled2_1 #24 | 2456-2460 | `OB-22` | the NE2000 invalid-TX log flood at 2459-2460 | `qhnetxlog` LOW, lines 2459-2460; 2731-2732: "an invalid NE2000 transmit span emits an unlatched WARNING" |
| ifiled2_1 #26 | 2614-2615 | `armthumbabortkill` | the PPC slow-path ifetch exit, `cpu_ppc_instr.c` | `qhslowifetch` HIGH, lines 2614-2615 scoped to PPC: "PPC slow ifetch still calls exit on a failed instruction read, separate from the Thumb stops already filed as armthumbabortkill" |
| ifiled2_1 #27 | 2616 | `m88kexit` | the PPC MSR.IP reboot hack; the `dev_mb89352` fatal errors (agy cited `cpu_ppc.c:166` and `dev_mb89352.c:266`; **[v2]** neither is a stop site at `c29a5fd3` -- the MSR.IP stop is `cpu_ppc.c:288-291`, and `dev_mb89352.c:266` is an executable assignment, `d->xferp->data_out_offset = d->transfer_bufpos;` -- **[v3]** v2 called it a comment; the comment ends at `:265` --; the MB89352 stops are the nine `cpu->running = 0` assignments (ten stop messages: EXBF's write and read share one; **[v3]** v2 said "ten ... sites") listed in `briefs/grok_mbstops.md`) | `qhppciphack` HIGH, line 2616, carries the PPC half.  **[v2] WRONG IN PART (Astra):** `qhm88kstops` HIGH carries ONLY the `:146` stop (a data-register read with no transfer object); the passage says "dev_mb89352 fatal errors", and `:169`/`:235`/`:290` (unimplemented phase), `:176`/`:242` (over-long transfer; `b120`'s text cites `:176`), `:312`/`:533`/`:690` (unimplemented LEN/SCMD/READ, live because `mb89352_abort_on_unimplemented_stuff` is `const bool ... = true`) are named by no row's title.  grok rules whether a row is owed and for which sites. |
| ifiled2_3 #28 | 16997-17000 | `xscalecp6exits`, `armendianexit` | the `arm_coproc_xscale_14()` exit at `cpu_arm_coproc.c:528`; the `arm_coproc_15()` non-endian exit at `:62` | `armcp15cp14exits` (ledger, open; **[v3]** filed by `#554` at `1202d342` from queue lines 18721-18722, not by `#555`): "the three remaining sibling exits of cpu_arm_coproc.c: :62 CP15 Rd==PC, :264 CP15 PID, :528 CP14 unknown" |

So: **four of the five lost no open item; the fifth (#27) may have -- grok's ruling decides** **[v2]**.  The brief
defect stands for all five: the generator (`mk_agy_idless2.py.txt`): a passage with
both a pointer and a new row was presented with the pointer alone (it was the BRIEF GENERATOR, `mk_agy_idless2.py.txt`, that listed the pointer only).  A re-run would list every id the table gives a
passage.  Nothing in the queue text or the ledger changes.

## The eleven OWED flags: disclosed debt under live rows

`ikeep2` part 1 asked for `OWED` on any passage "that says something is still open ... whose work is not done at
`c29a5fd3`, whatever the ruling says".  Items 8-18 are exactly the entries `#555` ruled KEEP-AS-IS because an existing
row already records the open work -- the governing lines quoted in the brief already read `OPEN: YES ...
DISPOSITION: KEEP-AS-IS` -- so agy's OWED restates the table: the work is open, and a row carries it.  **[v2]** v1 called
all eleven "disclosed clause-(e) residuals" and said a live carrier "owes nothing"; Astra corrected both: clause (e)
distinguishes a declared exclusion from a contract breach and a row's being live exempts nothing, and not all eleven
are clause-(e) debt (#8 is a host-portability qualification, several others are expressly named measurements).  The
test that was actually applied, and that Astra confirmed per item, is narrower and sufficient: **each residual is
recorded, in those words, in its carrier row's own queue text** (#8 at `c29a5fd3:OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:17805-17808`; #9 at
`:19530-19539`; #10-14 at `:19546-19566`; #15-18 at `:19568-19594`), so `#555` dropped nothing and no second filing is
owed.  Whether the carrier owes the work is the carrier's question, not `#555`'s.  The four carriers (ledger at
`c29a5fd3`):

| carrier | state | flags carried |
|---|---|---|
| `armbfiwidth` | open | #8 (the `1U` / `0xffffffffU` shift masks, `cpu_arm_instr.c:1351, 1411`) |
| `xscaleinten` | in work | #9 (undriven `rd == k` and the exact inten value, `xscale_inten_probe.py:14-16`) |
| `ppcrldimimask` | in work | #10-#14 (the SH=63/MB=1 row; the SH=40/MB=40 alias row; CR0 on Rc=1; the settling run; `R_NOGUARD`) |
| `mapledmaaddr` | in work | #15-#18 (the `timeout != 0` cell; the counter/selector/mask measurements; the no-maple binary; the silence control) |

**Nothing is owed by `#555` for these eleven.**  **[v2]** (v1 said here that a disclosed residual under a live row
"becomes a finding only when its carrier closes with the residual undone"; that made closure the only trigger, which is
not the rule -- the carrier owes its recorded work whenever its round runs.  What `closeassessrows` watches is the
narrower case of a row CLOSED on an assess sign-off with such work still named.)

Part 2 (entries left UNSETTLED): #19 the SH-4A software manual and #21 the AltiVec PEM are not in `_scratchpad/` (both
already on the owner's fetch list); #20 (the luna88k spin) names what would settle it; #22 says an 8254 silicon test or
an Intel note would settle the bare-count-write question and the datasheet (`i8254.txt:334`) leaves it undefined --
consistent with the row's UNSETTLED ruling.  No change.

