59:    #  *** THIS WAS A RAW SUBSTRING TEST OVER THE WHOLE FILE, AND THE GATE WENT GREEN OVER
60:    #  EXACTLY THE STATE IT EXISTS TO REDDEN. ***  Found 2026-08-21 by the flagship seat in a
61:    #  batched regress pass: check_fable_queue printed
62:    #        ok    sh4pcicexit    regress   owed and queued
63:    #  while the ONLY occurrence of that id in fable_queue.md was a PARENTHETICAL CROSS-REFERENCE
64:    #  on line 217, inside a different entry ("...one-instruction kills remain in the same file
65:    #  (`sh4pcicexit`)").  A MENTION satisfied "named in the queue" -- so the round with the worst
66:    #  detector prior in this project's history (seven of seven mutants escaped, one reinstating
67:    #  a host kill) had its regress review silently recorded as owed-and-queued when nothing was
68:    #  written down at all.
69:    #
70:    #  The fix idiom already existed three files away and had already been paid for: gate_offline's
71:    #  SM/SC manifests match stems EXACTLY in a loop, after being bitten by "a stem that is merely
72:    #  a prefix of another" (gate_offline.sh:1019-1023).  This is the same genus one directory up.
73:    #
74:    #  So an id counts as queued in exactly TWO places, and prose is not one of them:
