48:* **codex** -- a genuine OUTAGE, now DISCHARGED. It hit its usage limit and echoed eleven
49:  briefs; on 2026-08-20 it answered a health test and all eleven were re-fired against
50:  byte-identical briefs and verified real. Only the older 08-17/08-18 panels remain.
51:* **opus5 / fable5** -- NOT an outage. Both are alive and answering. They are held by an
52:  **owner allocation**: Opus DRIVES (implementing rounds) and Fable ADJUDICATES (it delivered
53:  the drop docket), with Fable deprioritised as a review seat. The nine cluster panels fired
54:  panel.sh's seven scriptable seats only, so those assess stages are 7/9 or 8/9.
